{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/429101-merit-idea-clan-archetype-condition","id":429101,"title":"[Merit Idea] Clan Archetype Condition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-05T12:05:28-08:00","id":429101,"title":"[Merit Idea] Clan Archetype Condition","content":"This is an idea I've had stuck in my head for a while. You see, I was reading through D:tD, and I liked the idea of Agenda Conditions. Basically, at the start of every chapter you get the Condition of any Agendas(D:tD's &quot;Y-Splat&quot;) you belong to. Once per chapter you can gain a Beat from it or resolve it for a +3 to a type of rolls(i.e., the Saboteurs gain a Beat whenever they're noticed after destabilizing a system, and can Resolve it to gain +3 to any roll provided they've taken steps to cause chaos beforehand). While this is nice, Covenants aren't quite Archetypical enough to simplify into a Condition. Clans, on the the other hand, are. My idea would be to make this a Merit, representing a particular resonance with your Clan's style of monstrousness. For example, a Mekhet might be able to gain a Beat once per chapter when they chose to act Mekkhet-esque( sticking to the shadows, being secretive, knowing more than they should), even when it would hinder them, and could resolve it to gain +3 to any Mental Skill roll(because the Shadow has seen enough that they know far more than they should). Figure it might be priced around two dots, with another Merit at the same price(requiring the other as a prereq) that allows you to Resolve it twice per chapter. So, anyone think this might be a good idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T12:39:47-08:00","id":429167,"title":"","content":"I'd argue for Covenant Conditions, because like the Agendas, they entail philosophy or ideas that a character opts into. You could be Embraced by a Mekhet but not share the culture of the clan at all, whereas your choice of Covenant is almost always more of a choice than your Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:12:08-08:00","id":429201,"title":"","content":"I actually really like this as Clan thing. Something simple that only a Shadow could do, or only a Lord. Might have to steal this the next time I run Requiem...<br /> <br /> It also reminds me of the little Clan gifts that they got in Danse Macabre, which I was slightly disappointed didn't end up in Second Ed. I mean, ultimately, Clan archetype is already enforced by Bane and Disciplines, but I like the idea of a little edge every clan gets to bring to the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:26:25-08:00","id":429213,"title":"","content":"Every clan except Ventrue already gets a clan specific merit that rewards them for playing up their clan's cliche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T15:04:34-08:00","id":429325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/106196-ventrue-specific-merit?p=107577#post107577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Heart of the Challenger (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Ventrue<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Your Lord's Beast stands as a gargoyle perched upon a parapet, ready to strike against any that would assail her. When any character unleashes the Predatory Aura on your character, that character gains the Competitive Condition, unless he achieves an Exceptional Success on the roll. If he already has the Competitive Condition, it becomes Persistent, and can only be resolved by besting your character in a competition where the character lost a Humanity/Integrity dot.<br /> Once per scene, you can take +3 dice against any single character with the Competitive Condition, as if you'd spent a point of Willpower. You cannot spend Willpower to add additional dice to such a roll. This counts toward the Competitive Condition's requirement for spending Willpower.<br /> Note that this Merit supersedes the normal monthly limitation on the Competitive Condition.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Your character suffers the Competitive Condition at all times. It cannot be resolved. However, when it would normally be resolved, gain a Beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stole this from another thread, but yeah...the Venture have one too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T17:04:52-08:00","id":429486,"title":"","content":"Homebrewed material doesn't count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T17:12:17-08:00","id":429491,"title":"","content":"@Audrey St. John: It appears to be written by one of the Freelancers, so I'm not sure if I'd label it Homebrew.<br /> <br /> @Leetsepeak: Though I intended that the Merit would be bought by those who DO buy into their Clan culture, a good point. My only issue is that it's harder to boil down the Covenants into singular Conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T17:41:14-08:00","id":429513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/429101-merit-idea-clan-archetype-condition?p=429491#post429491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Audrey St. John: It appears to be written by one of the Freelancers, so I'm not sure if I'd label it Homebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not in the book, so it's definitely in the homebrew territory. That's not a slight against it in my view, it just is what it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/429101-merit-idea-clan-archetype-condition?p=429491#post429491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Leetsepeak: Though I intended that the Merit would be bought by those who DO buy into their Clan culture, a good point. My only issue is that it's harder to boil down the Covenants into singular Conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that, given Agendas don't provide any other concrete benefits, and Covenant and Clan both provide tangible benefits besides Conditions, there's a pretty decent reason for there to be little need for either to have a Condition associated with them.<br /> <br /> I'd just use the Tasked Condition coming from sires/clanmates/covenants if you want to involve characters in the group and reward it with Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T17:50:52-08:00","id":429519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/429101-merit-idea-clan-archetype-condition?p=429213#post429213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every clan except Ventrue already gets a clan specific merit that rewards them for playing up their clan's cliche.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if they couldn't have updated the book when they redid it officially as second edition, because there's multiple threads regarding this topic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T02:52:39-08:00","id":431157,"title":"","content":"I like this as a Clan thing. The blood shapes you a little, and this nicely might give a small bonus. <br /> <br /> I'll consider this for my current game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:04:02-08:00","id":431507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/429101-merit-idea-clan-archetype-condition?p=429513#post429513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not in the book, so it's definitely in the homebrew territory. That's not a slight against it in my view, it just is what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, yeah, but in this particular case it's important to note that it is Homebrew written by Dave H, the person who wrote all of the Merits in the book, who has specifically said he meant to include an exclusive Merit for each Clan but that one got left out due to an oversight, and by the time it's absence was noticed it was too late to put back in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}